#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Capture the published visual/CPU suite with reviewable bounds and isolated app groups.

init ROOT [--rival-manifest JSON] [--flea-bin PATH --anchor-bin PATH]
fixtures ROOT --raw-corpus DIR generate non-RAW media and copy verified real RAW sets
dry-run ROOT                  inventory and write the complete, unranked run plan
run ROOT --raw-corpus DIR [--only IDS --installed] capture selected entrant trials
report ROOT                   validate annotations.json and emit results.json/results.csv
selftest ROOT                 check bounds, coverage, quiet/rebound and ranking contracts

ROOT must be a canonical directory with its own .flea-test-sandbox marker. No cleanup
or cache deletion occurs. Every trial has private HOME/XDG directories and a private
D-Bus session inside its cgroup, including activated thumbnailers. The field-search
tool supplies the existing native input, session and window inspection primitives.
Visual judgments belong in annotations.json, referencing adjacent captured frames.
No pixel-change, CPU-quiet or thumbnail-cache heuristic stands in for visual review.
The gate covers historical B1 only; the release's full coverage belongs to its campaign ledger.
"""
